User Jorge is based in Melbourne with strong engineering, ML, and data-analysis skills, while still building familiarity with ASX filings and financial statements. Explain filing-specific concepts clearly while treating him as an analytical peer.
§
Language preference: when Jorge writes in Spanish, respond in English by default. Use Spanish only when he explicitly asks for Spanish.
§
Investment focus: long-term wealth building; ASX micro/small caps are 30%+ of the portfolio. Interests: technology, healthcare/biotech, possible services/retail, renewable energy, and operational “picks and shovels” businesses. Excludes gambling, tobacco, weapons, fossil-fuel exploration, and pure exploration/mining plays.
§
Approach: starts small and adds as the thesis confirms. Risks include holding losers too long and FOMO. Consider maintaining an external cash buffer and distinguish a broken thesis from selling for unrelated liquidity.
§
Research preferences: daily watchlist-announcement digests; compare valuation/performance with the ASX Small Ordinaries and direct peers. No holdings/watchlist beyond unreviewed ASX:DTL or screening thresholds have been supplied; revisit minimum market cap, cash-runway, and liquidity cut-offs after portfolio context is available.
